 hook keeps `selection = { mode: 'new' }` instead of resetting and auto-selecting workspace B's most-recent session. The UI stays stuck in \"new session\" mode for the wrong workspace — `isNewSessionMode` stays true, `selectedSessionId` stays `undefined`, and `sessions[0]` for the new workspace is silently ignored, even though the comment at line 54 says \"Always select first session when sessions are available for this workspace.\"\n\n```json\n{\"file\": \"packages/web-core/src/shared/hooks/useWorkspaceSessions.ts\", \"line\": 57, \"defect\": \"The workspace-change check (prevWorkspaceIdRef comparison) was deleted, so `prev?.mode === 'new'` now short-circuits regardless of whether workspaceId actually changed.\", \"effect\": \"Switching to a different workspace while in new-session mode leaves the UI stuck showing the new-session form instead of auto-selecting that workspace's most recent existing session.\"}\n```","ttft_ms":1159,"type":"result","duration_ms":14348,"uuid":"86512905-594c-49a9-aa94-c64624814721","ttft_stream_ms":781,"time_to_request_ms":46,"first_content_frame_ms":781,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
